{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Scott Edward Adkins (born 17 June 1976) is an English actor and martial artist who is best known for playing Russian prison fighter Yuri Boyka in the 2006 film "" and its following two sequels: "" (2010) and "" (2016) and Casey Bowman in Ninja and its sequel .","title":"Scott Adkins"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is also known for playing Bradley Hume in "Holby City", Lucian in "Doctor Strange", Kiley in "The Bourne Ultimatum" and John in "Zero Dark Thirty".","title":"Scott Adkins"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Adkins has also appeared in "EastEnders", "Hollyoaks", "Doctors" as well as starred in many direct-to-video films.","title":"Scott Adkins"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Universal Soldier franchise is a series of science fiction action films.","title":"Universal Soldier (franchise)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The franchise began in 1992 with "Universal Soldier" and as of 2012 comprises six entries (some of which are now considered non-canon).","title":"Universal Soldier (franchise)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The films centered on the character of Luc Deveraux (played first by Jean-Claude Van Damme and then by Matt Battaglia) until "", which focuses on a new protagonist named John (played by Scott Adkins).","title":"Universal Soldier (franchise)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Universal Soldier is a 1992 American military science fiction action film directed by Roland Emmerich, produced by Mario Kassar and Allen Shapiro, and written by Richard Rothstein and Dean Devlin.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film tells the story of Luc Deveraux, a former US Army soldier who was killed in Vietnam War in 1969, and returned to life following a secret military project called the "Universal Soldier" program.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" However, he finds out about his past even although his memory was erased, and escapes alongside a young TV journalist.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Along the way, they have to deal with the return of his archenemy, Sgt. Andrew Scott, who had lost his sanity in the Vietnam War, and became a psychotic megalomaniac, intent on killing him and leading the Universal Soldiers.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "Universal Soldier" was released by TriStar Pictures on July 10, 1992.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The film grossed $36 million worldwide against its budget of $23 million.","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It spawned a series of films, including several rather poorly received direct-to-TV films: "", which has since been removed from the series canon, followed by "" and "".","title":"Universal Soldier (1992 film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Zero Dark Thirty" is a 2012 American action thriller directed and co-produced by Kathryn Bigelow with screenplay by Mark Boal.","title":"List of accolades received by Zero Dark Thirty"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film was released in the United States on December 19, 2012, with a limited release at five theaters in Los Angeles and New York City.","title":"List of accolades received by Zero Dark Thirty"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It made $124,848 in its limited release weekend, making it one of the biggest limited mid-week openings ever.","title":"List of accolades received by Zero Dark Thirty"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As of March 6, 2013, "Zero Dark Thirty" has grossed a worldwide total of $106.8 million.","title":"List of accolades received by Zero Dark Thirty"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "Zero Dark Thirty" also received a high critical acclaim, accumulating an approval rating of 93% on the review aggregator site Rotten Tomatoes.","title":"List of accolades received by Zero Dark Thirty"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Luc Deveraux is a fictional character and the protagonist of the "Universal Soldier" film series.","title":"Luc Deveraux"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is most famously portrayed by Belgian actor and martial artist Jean-Claude Van Damme.","title":"Luc Deveraux"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Van Damme portrays Luc in the 1992 film "Universal Soldier" and its sequels "" (1999), "" (2009), and "" (2012); he is portrayed by Matt Battaglia in the direct-to-video sequels "" (1998) and "" (1998).","title":"Luc Deveraux"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jayne Grayson is a fictional character in the BBC medical drama "Holby City", portrayed by actress Stella Gonet.","title":"Jayne Grayson"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The character first appeared on-screen on 10 July 2007 in episode "Under the Radar" - series 9, episode 39 of the programme.","title":"Jayne Grayson"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Her role in the show was that of Chief Executive Officer of the Holby City Hospital Primary Care Trust, making her the only regular character who is not a medic by profession.","title":"Jayne Grayson"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Gonet formerly appeared as a doctor in "Holby City"<nowiki>'</nowiki>s sister show "Casualty", and has since appeared in crossover episodes of the drama, this time as Jayne Grayson.","title":"Jayne Grayson"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Her storylines in "Holby City" have revolved around issues of hospital bureaucracy, as well as her husband's affair with her colleague Connie Beauchamp.","title":"Jayne Grayson"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" A two-part episode which saw Jayne fight the hospital's Board of Directors and the British government over the separation surgery of the conjoined twin daughters of illegal Korean immigrants proved a critical success, and was positively received by many tabloid TV critics.","title":"Jayne Grayson"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Scott Adkins
